## Faithful Printing Error

One author-identified erratum, preserved by native finalization:
p0232-math-1, block p0232#3, original "$a\ne0$".
The source definition visibly prints a(a>0,a!=0); the necessary crop confirms
0 rather than1. The source text remains unchanged.
a=1 meets the printed conditions but makes 1^x=1 nonunique and 1^x=b for
b!=1 unsolvable. The previous source text and this page's later general
condition explicitly exclude1. Thus the erroneous excluded value is
uniquely identified as0 instead of1; the reason is registered, not silently
corrected in SOURCE. This author finding is not an independent review.
No other erratum or mathematical alteration was introduced.

